  /* When compiled with OpenMP, use a single parallel region.
     The outer loop over i remains logically sequential; inside each
     iteration:
       - One thread (omp single) computes the lower part of row i.
       - All threads (omp for) cooperate to compute the upper part.
     The barriers implied by 'single' and 'for' keep all threads
     synchronized on the current value of i, preserving the original
     dependences exactly. */
